 "title": "One-Gadget",
 "desc": "Goal: A \"one-gadget\" is a single address in libc that, when jumped to, executes execve(\"/bin/sh\") — no ROP chain needed! You find them with the one_gadget tool. Each has constraints (e.g., RAX==NULL, [RSP+0x30]==NULL) that must be satisfied.",
